    dict(key='06-act-2', kind='console', title='Act Two — Node<T>: data is a reference',
         body='TWO. Node<T>: data is a reference.\n  count() = 6: 6 steps; each Node<Clue> holds a reference to a Clue and a next pointer\n  head.data is the Clue object the oak tree (40 m); the node points at it, it does not contain a copy',
         narration='What does a node hold? [[slnc 400]] Two references. [[slnc 300]] One to the clue, which lives elsewhere in memory. [[slnc 300]] And one to the next node. [[slnc 500]] The node does not contain a copy of the clue. [[slnc 300]] It points at it. [[slnc 400]] Counting is still six steps along the next pointers.'),
